The clade '''Feraequornithes''' was named by Sangster & Mayr, 2021 to include the '''[[Pelecanimorphae]]''' and '''[[Austrodyptornithes|Procellariimorphae]]''' to the exclusion of the loons ('''[[Gaviiformes]]'''). They defined this clade in the ''PhyloCode'' as "the least inclusive clade containing ''[[Pelecanus onocrotalus]]'' and ''[[Procellaria aequinoctialis]]''".<ref name="sangster&mayr"/>

